# From "Free Flow 10" (Wave I - Discovery, CD3-6): a bare frame for
# whatever purpose the listener set for themselves before beginning, rather
# than content of its own. Distinct from free.gws (a generic hold used at
# F12/F15/F21/F27) -- this one is F10-specific and names the purpose.

@segment  free-flow-10
@title    Free Flow — Your Own Purpose
@levels   F10
@duration ~5m

say This is your own exercise, for whatever you came here to do.
pause 5
say Remember the purpose you set before you began. Now, in Focus 10, carry it out.
pause 8
say Take the time you need.
hold 300
